  "worked_solution": "For a curve $r(t)=\u27e8x(t),y(t),z(t)\u27e9$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{\u2032}(t)}{\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82,\\,2t,\\,\\frac{1}{t}\u27e9 \\\\ {r}^{\u2032}(1) & =\u27e82,\\,2(1),\\,\\frac{1}{1}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82,2,1\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{\u2032}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(1)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(2)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4+1} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{\u2032}(1)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{\u2032}(1)}{\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(1)\u2016} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\u27e82,2,1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{3}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
